        </qual:listOfFunctionTerms>
      </qual:transition>
      <qual:transition qual:id="tr_S_7">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p key="P_regulatorysummary_0" contentType="RegulatorySummary">p38 was shown to bind to MEF2C and increase MEF2C transcriptional activity.</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_0">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">11796223</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_1" contentType="RegulatorySummary">R-smads coregulate MEF2C activity by direct binding. TGF-beta1, via Smad3 represses MEF2C -dependant transcription while the Smad complex would increase the activity. (! reference not chondrocyte specific)</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_1">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">11160896</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">11796223</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">15044954</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_2" contentType="RegulatorySummary">PTHrP signalling induces dephosphorylation of histone deacetylase 4 (HDAC4), which promotes nuclear translocation of HDAC4 and repression of MEF2 transcriptional activity.</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_2">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">25529628</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">19704004</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_3" contentType="RegulatorySummary">HDAC4 has a repressive effect on MEF2C-dependant expression of Runx2</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_3">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">20951345</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">11796223</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">22971952</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">15537544</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_4" contentType="RegulatorySummary">p38 is required for hypetrophic chondrocyte differentiation, its function would be mediated by MEF2C transcription factor</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_4">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">18546337</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">14594450</span></li></ul></body>
        </notes>
        <qual:listOfInputs>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_7_in_S_33" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_33" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
