      <qual:transition qual:id="tr_S_37">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p key="P_regulatorysummary_0" contentType="RegulatorySummary">Dlx5 would be indispensable for BMP2-induced Runx2 expression, its transcriptional activity is promoted by BMP2 signalling (SmadComplex) but not TGFbeta (Smad2/3)</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_0">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">22253449</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">16901655</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">12815054</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_1" contentType="RegulatorySummary">p38: Dlx5 would mediate BMP2-induced expression of osteocytes target genes. Moreover, Dlx5 would be substrate of p38 MAPK. Phosphorylation by p38 increases the transactivation potential of Dlx5 (NB: In vitro phosphorylation assay, C2C12 (mouse premyoblasts) and HEK-293 (Human embryonic kidney cells))</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_1">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">18056716</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_2" contentType="RegulatorySummary">Msx2 and Dlx5 form an heterodimer, they binds via their respective DNA binding sites and antagonise each other's transcriptional activity</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_2">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">22253449</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">9111364</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">15456894</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">16314053</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_3" contentType="RegulatorySummary">p38 MAPK phosphorylates DLX5 and therefore increases its transcriptional activity by promoting its association with the transcriptional co-activator p300. This was shown particularly for C2C12 cells.</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_3">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">18056716</span></li></ul></body>
        </notes>
        <qual:listOfInputs>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_37_in_S_33" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_33" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_37_in_S_22" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_22" qual:sign="negative" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_37_in_S_44" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_44" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
        </qual:listOfInputs>
        <qual:listOfOutputs>
          <qual:output qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_37" qual:transitionEffect="assignmentLevel"/>
        </qual:listOfOutputs>
