                <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
              </apply>
            </math>
                    </qual:functionTerm>
        </qual:listOfFunctionTerms>
      </qual:transition>
      <qual:transition qual:id="tr_S_55">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p key="P_regulatorysummary_0" contentType="RegulatorySummary">Wnt pathway is inhibited by its antagonist DKK1 with receptor binding competition (Frizzled-LRP5/6 transduces Wnt pathway)</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_0">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">22576962</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_1" contentType="RegulatorySummary">Activated by Wnt binding</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_1">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">21536751</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">17659995</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_2" contentType="RegulatorySummary">In the ON state, a Wnt ligand binds to the seven-pass transmembrane receptor Frizzled (FZD) and the single-pass low-density lipoprotein receptor-related protein 5 or 6 (LRP5/6)</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_2">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">DOI</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi">10.1242/dev.01117</span><span class="pmid"/></li><li>
                <span class="referType">DOI</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi">10.1101/cshperspect.a007880</span><span class="pmid"/></li></ul></body>
        </notes>
        <qual:listOfInputs>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_55_in_S_12" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_12" qual:sign="negative" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_55_in_S_50" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_50" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
        </qual:listOfInputs>
        <qual:listOfOutputs>
          <qual:output qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_55" qual:transitionEffect="assignmentLevel"/>
        </qual:listOfOutputs>
        <qual:listOfFunctionTerms>
          <qual:defaultTerm qual:resultLevel="0">
          </qual:defaultTerm>
          <qual:functionTerm qual:resultLevel="1">
            <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">            
              <apply>
                <eq/>
                <ci> S_50 </ci>
                <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
              </apply>
            </math>
                    </qual:functionTerm>
        </qual:listOfFunctionTerms>
      </qual:transition>
      <qual:transition qual:id="tr_S_56">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p key="P_regulatorysummary_0" contentType="RegulatorySummary">GSK3B would affect HDAC4 stability via post-trancriptional modification and subsequent proteosome degradation (! refrence not chondrocyte specific)</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_0">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">21118993</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_1" contentType="RegulatorySummary">PP2A, which is activated by PKA, promotes dephosphorylation of HDAC4, which translocates into the nucleus and represses the activity of MEF2 transcription factors, ultimately attenuating the rate of chondrocyte hypertrophy</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_1">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">22971952</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">19704004</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">25715393</span></li></ul></body>
        </notes>
        <qual:listOfInputs>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_56_in_S_53" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_53" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_56_in_S_52" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_52" qual:sign="negative" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
        </qual:listOfInputs>
        <qual:listOfOutputs>
          <qual:output qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_56" qual:transitionEffect="assignmentLevel"/>
        </qual:listOfOutputs>
        <qual:listOfFunctionTerms>
          <qual:defaultTerm qual:resultLevel="0">
          </qual:defaultTerm>
          <qual:functionTerm qual:resultLevel="1">
            <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">            
              <apply>
                <eq/>
                <ci> S_53 </ci>
                <cn type="integer"> 1 </cn>
              </apply>
            </math>
                    </qual:functionTerm>
        </qual:listOfFunctionTerms>
      </qual:transition>
      <qual:transition qual:id="tr_S_57">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p key="P_regulatorysummary_0" contentType="RegulatorySummary">Activation of EGF following ligand binding leads to activation of the PI3K/Akt pathway activation via Ras phosphorylation. Ras directly binds to PI3K.</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_0">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">8665852</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_1" contentType="RegulatorySummary">IGFI regulates chondrocytes differentiation and maintenance of differenitated phenotype through the activation of phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase (PI3K) and Akt</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_1">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">19319849</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">12853454</span></li></ul><p key="P_regulatorysummary_2" contentType="RegulatorySummary">IL-1beta signalling activates downstream pathways including the Pi3K/Akt one</p><ul key="P_regulatorysummary_2">
              <li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">32189997</span></li><li>
                <span class="referType">PMID</span><span class="position">0</span><span class="doi"/><span class="pmid">28320092</span></li></ul></body>
        </notes>
        <qual:listOfInputs>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_57_in_S_18" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_18" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_57_in_S_15" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_15" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
          <qual:input qual:id="tr_S_57_in_S_13" qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_13" qual:sign="positive" qual:thresholdLevel="1" qual:transitionEffect="none"/>
        </qual:listOfInputs>
        <qual:listOfOutputs>
          <qual:output qual:qualitativeSpecies="S_57" qual:transitionEffect="assignmentLevel"/>
        </qual:listOfOutputs>
